Let me read switching.rs directly around drive_windows.
{"findings":[{"severity":"MINOR","file":"crates/vigilode/src/switching.rs","line":1047,"claim":"C1 says sentinel state changes match the ordinary recheck path. They don't for the re-arm memory. On a losing sentinel, implicit_rate_at_discard is set to the rate of the same window that was just measured (implicit_rate was overwritten at line 1025). The ordinary path stores the rate from before the recheck (line 1298). The sentinel window's own rate also skips the re-arm test at lines 1532-1540.","scenario":"Legacy config (entry_probe_adaptation None), rearm_rate_ratio 2. An earlier recheck was discarded with stored rate R_old=1000. At the next due recheck the window costs 400 per unit time. Ordinary path: the probe is discarded and implicit_rate_at_discard = R_prev. The following RODAS batch then sees 400*2 <= R_prev, so it sets probe_discards=0 and since_probe=probe_interval, and the next recheck happens immediately. Sentinel path: probe_discards goes up by 1, so the recheck interval grows, and the anchor is overwritten with 400. That window can never trigger a re-arm, so the next recheck comes later than it would on the ordinary path.","suggested_fix":"Set implicit_rate_at_discard before overwriting implicit_rate, and run the ordinary re-arm test on the retained sentinel window's rate. Or document that sentinel follows the replay-path convention."},{"severity":"MINOR","file":"crates/vigilode/src/switching.rs","line":972,"claim":"A fatal explicit trial throws away an implicit window that completed successfully and that the policy itself calls the productive advance. This also differs from the ordinary fatal-probe path (line 1284-1286), which commits the probe's accepted prefix. So 'consistent with the ordinary path' only holds against the fatal-comparator path.","scenario":"session.rs:276-286 treats a nonfinite RHS output as callback_failure, so run() marks it fatal. Take a stiff Robertson-like window: RODAS completes [a,b]. The DOPRI trial's first step at h0=opts.h0 makes y2 huge, and the 3e7*y2^2 term overflows to inf. The trial becomes 'fatal sentinel explicit return'. The solve stops at final_time=a even though a valid accepted state at b was already computed and charged.","suggested_fix":"Commit the implicit window first, then stop with the fatal explicit message. Both records stay charged and only the implicit one is published. At minimum, record in the preregistration that sentinel fatal handling deliberately loses implicit progress."},{"severity":"MINOR","file":"crates/vigilode/src/switching.rs","line":961,"claim":"When the explicit trial returns Err (no work record), the code pushes an implicit record whose decision is the empty string \"\" and whose evidence is Uncompared. The completed implicit window is also not committed.","scenario":"run(Dopri5) returns Err, for example from Dopri5::with_session validation or OutputSchedule::new refusing [start,target,solve_end] near clock resolution. The result has a segment with decision=\"\", accounting_complete=false, and final_time left at start despite a successful charged implicit window.","suggested_fix":"Set a decision such as 'sentinel explicit return failed without work record; stop', and decide explicitly whether to commit the implicit window before breaking."},{"severity":"MINOR","file":"crates/vigilode/src/switching.rs","line":1022,"claim":"Misleading record. If the implicit window uses up the attempt budget (remaining==0 at line 933), no explicit trial runs. The implicit record is still tagged ImplicitPreferredOnSameWindow with decision 'sentinel implicit comparator retained as productive implicit advance', and tenure_rechecks/since_probe count it as a recheck that never happened.","scenario":"max_steps runs out exactly as the sentinel implicit window reaches target. The record claims a same-window comparison was won when there was no comparison at all.","suggested_fix":"When explicit is None, use ImplicitWindowCompleted and a decision like 'sentinel implicit window completed; budget left no explicit trial'."},{"severity":"MINOR","file":"crates/vigilode/src/switching.rs","line":939,"claim":"The sentinel's explicit trial has no attempt cap: local.max_steps = remaining. Its RHS ceiling scales with W_impl, and W_impl counts each Jacobian build as n units. So the cost of a discarded trial is not bounded by probe_attempt_budget the way an ordinary recheck is, and it draws on the global opts.max_steps.","scenario":"n=100 with dense Jacobians: a stiff window with 500 Jacobian builds has W ≈ 5e4 units. With ratio 0.8, the DOPRI trial may use about 4e4 RHS, roughly 6.7e3 attempts, and then be discarded. With k=1 and about 12 rechecks, a solve with max_steps=100000 can end on 'total attempt budget exhausted' where the default path (≤16 probe attempts per recheck) would finish.","suggested_fix":"Also cap the trial's attempts, e.g. max_steps = remaining.min(some multiple of the implicit window's attempts), or document the per-sentinel worst case of (1+ratio)·W_impl+8 units and the attempt-budget exposure as a known cost of the opt-in feature."},{"severity":"MINOR","file":"crates/vigilode/src/switching.rs","line":1228,"claim":"C2 feeds the lower bound in as a point interval [W,W] with admissible=true. This bypasses the OutputNotQualified guard in compare_qualified_costs and makes the evidence look like an observed point cost. The committed explicit record then carries ExplicitCheaperOnSameWindow and 'explicit return passed actual same-window work comparison' (line 1262), which looks the same as a comparison against a completed comparator.","scenario":"A downstream consumer, or the trace and analysis tools, filtering on evidence==ExplicitCheaperOnSameWindow will count lower-bound wins as completed same-window comparisons. Only the following replay segment's decision string tells them apart.","suggested_fix":"Encode the incomplete comparator as CostInterval{lower: W, upper: f64::INFINITY} (or a distinct CostEvidenceKind), and use a separate decision/evidence for the lower-bound win, e.g. 'passed same-window lower-bound comparison'."},{"severity":"MINOR","file":"crates/vigilode/tests/return_sentinel_contracts.rs","line":66,"claim":"The tests would pass even if the k-th-recheck logic were broken. Every sentinel test, and the pilot arm, uses return_sentinel_interval=1, so tenure_rechecks % 1 == 0 is always true. The increments at switching.rs:885/1178 and the resets at 1019/1283/1505 are never tested.","scenario":"Delete the tenure_rechecks reset at entry (line 1505), or the ordinary-path increment (line 1178): all 6 tests still pass. The paths with remaining==0 after the implicit window, an explicit Err, and the off-by-default bitwise identity (checked only by measurement gate G1) are also untested.","suggested_fix":"Add a k=2 test that checks sentinel and ordinary rechecks alternate within a tenure and that the count restarts after a return and re-entry. Add a cargo test that sentinel=0 gives segment records bitwise equal to the base config on one fixture."},{"severity":"MINOR","file":"research/adapter_checkpoint_followup_20261027/PREREGISTRATION.md","line":47,"claim":"E3 calls 'uninterrupted solve vs split batches' an upper bound on what session preservation could gain. That needs W_session >= W_uninterrupted, which nothing guarantees. Step-size control isn't monotone under landing clips, the relaxation fixture already shows −4.8%, and E3 uses the raw starting step where the adapter batches use implicit_seed. A real session would also change the measured implicit rates, and so the recheck schedule and tenure boundaries.","scenario":"A persistent RODAS session that keeps the controller and Jacobian state but must land on window endpoints can need fewer rejected steps than the unclipped solve, so it saves more than the stated 'upper bound'. Relaxation, where the uninterrupted solve is worse than split batches, is a direct example.","suggested_fix":"Call it a heuristic point estimate under the same tenure decisions, not an upper bound. Or measure a session that lands on window endpoints with the adapter's seeds."},{"severity":"NOTE","file":"crates/vigilode/src/switching.rs","line":951,"claim":"The sentinel cost bound holds as stated, with hidden assumptions. The ceiling is checked after each advance_to(...,1) against attempted RHS calls: dopri5.rs:355 increments before calling, so recoverable or failing calls count too. Hence record.rhs_calls ≤ floor(r·W)+1+7 (one 6-stage FSAL attempt plus the initial derivative). That relies on: h0 always being supplied (no step-size heuristic evaluations), FSAL on, work_units==rhs for DOPRI, and W_impl being in mixed units (Jacobian builds weighted ×n), so the RHS allowance is a unit-model heuristic, not a wall-cost bound. The cap never blocks a winning trial: a stop needs rhs−base ≥ floor(rW)+2 > rW ≥ the winning threshold.","scenario":"With fsal=false, or any future pre-base RHS evaluation, the margin over the cap grows by one or more RHS calls. The test's +7 slack would then fail even though the behavior is correct.","suggested_fix":"State the bound as floor(r·W)+1 + (RHS of one attempt) + (pre-base evaluations) and name the unit model."},{"severity":"NOTE","file":"crates/vigilode/src/switching.rs","line":1195,"claim":"The C2 lower bound is sound in the same sense as the existing completed-comparator rule, and no further. It assumes deterministic, replay-safe callbacks and that the budget-truncated run is a prefix of the unbounded run with the same h0=seed.min(target−start) and no landings. Counters only increase (rhs/jvp/ft/solves plus jac·n), replay has no ceiling, and terminal failures make completion impossible, so the bound holds trivially there. It does not bound the different run that would actually follow a discard: a coalesced batch with h0=seed.min(batch_target−start) and interior landings.","scenario":"Nonfatal stops include MaxStepsReached from implicit_pilot_attempt_budget (64) or from the global remaining budget, step-size underflow, and linear-solve failure. In every case the replay's work is ≤ the work of finishing that same deterministic run, so I found no counterexample where incomplete work exceeds completion cost.","suggested_fix":"Write the determinism/prefix assumption next to the rule in the code comment and the preregistration."},{"severity":"NOTE","file":"crates/vigilode/src/switching.rs","line":1284,"claim":"Pre-existing, outside this diff: the ordinary fatal-explicit-probe path commits the uncompared probe's accepted prefix. This contradicts the 'never publish a trial state' principle that the new sentinel and fatal-comparator paths follow.","scenario":"An explicit recheck that fails fatally mid-window publishes its accepted DOPRI prefix, although it never passed the return comparison.","suggested_fix":"Make all trial-fatal paths consistent, either all committing or all keeping the checkpoint."},{"severity":"NOTE","file":"crates/vigilode/src/switching.rs","line":894,"claim":"The sentinel implicit run is called with probe=true, so a committed productive implicit window has is_probe=true. This matches the retained-replay convention. Consumers that split trial work from productive work by is_probe will misclassify it. There is also one opts.clone() per sentinel (it allocates when atol is a vector), which goes against the 'one mutable copy' comment at line 830. Not a hot loop.","scenario":"An analysis summing is_probe work as overhead counts the committed sentinel implicit windows as overhead.","suggested_fix":"Pass probe=false for the sentinel implicit window, or document that is_probe means 'root of a comparison'. Reuse a second scratch Options instead of cloning."},{"severity":"NOTE","file":"crates/rodas5p-integrators/src/routing.rs","line":229,"claim":"Adding a public field to the public struct RoutingOptions (no #[non_exhaustive]) breaks semver for downstream code that builds it with a struct literal. Every literal in this workspace uses ..Default, so nothing here breaks. solve.rs ENTRY_ROUTED still records 'integrate_rodas5p_routed_observed' although the call is now _with_options with non-default options. With a non-GMRES matrix_free config, krylov_ls_workspace=true would call gmres.set_ls_workspace(true) while the record says krylov-ws-legacy-v1. The facade can't reach that combination.","scenario":"An external crate with `RoutingOptions { matrix_free: cfg }` stops compiling. A reader of route.entry_point cannot see which options were used except through driver_work.krylov_workspace.","suggested_fix":"Add #[non_exhaustive] or document the API break. Optionally record the options in the route record."}],"refuted_claims":["C1 'state transitions consistent with the ordinary recheck/return path' holds only in part: the sentinel's implicit_rate_at_discard anchor and missing re-arm test differ from the ordinary non-replay path (switching.rs:1047), and its fatal-explicit handling discards a completed implicit window, unlike the ordinary fatal-probe path, which commits (switching.rs:972 vs 1284).","Prereg E3 'upper bound on what a complete RODAS session could save' is a heuristic estimate, not a bound (non-monotone step control under landings, different h0, decision feedback; the relaxation −4.8% shows the non-monotonicity).","Claim that every k-th recheck is a sentinel and the counter restarts each tenure: correct by reading, but the tests never exercise it because all of them use k=1."],"confirmed_claims":["C1: every trial is charged exactly once (implicit at line 914, explicit at line 969, before any fatal/discard branch); a discarded or rejected explicit trial never touches result.final_state, entry memory or the persistent session (scoped session, rooted at the uncommitted checkpoint).","C1: no infinite or zero-progress loop. target<=final_time is skipped, remaining==0 breaks before the trial, probe is cleared, a successful implicit or winning explicit window ends at target, and an implicit window with W=0 gives ceiling 1, so DOPRI stops after one attempt and the implicit window commits.","C1: the explicit trial's RHS is at most floor(r·W)+1 plus one DOPRI attempt (≤7 RHS, initial derivative included); attempted calls are counted, and the cap never blocks a trial that would have won.","C1: fatal or incomplete sentinel implicit windows stop exactly like an ordinary implicit batch (accepted prefix committed); a fatal explicit trial publishes neither record.","C2: the work of a nonfatal incomplete comparator is a valid lower bound on completing the same deterministic replay (counters only increase, no ceiling, a budget stop is a prefix), so an explicit win against r times that bound is also a win against r times the true cost. With incomplete comparators, the old code always fell through to Incomparable, so only cells with an incomplete replay can change.","C3: for every input that reaches the facade's matrix-free route (JVP-only, scalar atol, no declared band, no dense output, default GMRES config), the ls-workspace entry differs from the legacy entry only in set_ls_workspace/set_krylov_workspace(ls_workspace()). gmres_into is already true, set_krylov_workspace cannot fail for GMRES, and the m<n case falls back to the allocating solve. States, counters and partials are the same driver loop; only the krylov_workspace id changes. Vector atol, a declared band and dense output are routed elsewhere, and LGMRES/GCRODR configs can't be reached from the facade."]}
